                <pb facs="1039" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119T&amp;M/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Special Mission at
                        Lausanne</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-07T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. Your 64, December 6, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>I am much gratified at the manner in which you have presented this Government’s
                    views in regard to the question of the freedom of the Straits.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
